---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/editions.css';
import catalog from '../data/edition-catalog.mjs';
---
<BaseLayout locale="en" title="Private Studio Editor">
 <section class="editions">
  <span class="eyebrow">Studio administration</span><h1>Studio Editor</h1><p class="intro">Manage collections, edition prices, collector requests and the mailing list in one place.</p><p id="status" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="small"><a href="/editions-editor/preview/">Collector Experience ↗</a></p>
  <form id="login" class="panel"><h2>Studio sign-in</h2><p class="small">Connect here to edit live prices and requests. Use a GitHub access token belonging to ClaytonTalmon, with access to the website repository. For collection publishing, choose Contents: Read and write. Your token stays only in this window and is cleared on sign-out; it is never saved with drafts. Your secure studio session lasts eight hours.</p><label>GitHub access token<input name="token" type="password" autocomplete="off" required /></label><button class="primary">Open the editor</button></form>
  <div id="studio" hidden>
   <div class="studio-actions"><button id="logout">Sign out</button><a href="https://talmonphoto.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View website ↗</a></div>
   <nav class="studio-tabs" aria-label="Studio sections">
    <button type="button" data-section="collections" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="panel-collections">Collections</button>
    <button type="button" data-section="prices" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="panel-prices">Edition Prices</button>
    <button type="button" data-section="requests" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="panel-requests">Collector Requests</button>
    <button type="button" data-section="mailing" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="panel-mailing">Mailing List</button>
   </nav>
   <section id="panel-collections" data-studio-panel="collections">
    <h2>Collections &amp; Process</h2><p class="small">Arrange photographs, edit titles and print details, or update the Process page. Save a draft to keep work in progress; Publish updates the website after its rebuild. Existing draft files can be opened with Load draft file.</p>
    <iframe id="collection-editor-frame" title="Collection and Process editor" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"></iframe>
   </section>
   <section id="panel-prices" data-studio-panel="prices" class="panel" hidden><h2>Edition prices</h2><p class="small">Choose Entire collection to set prices for every photograph in a collection, or Individual photograph for exceptions and sales counts. Collection pricing replaces existing prices for the selected format while preserving each photograph’s number sold. Prices apply to pairs of numbered prints: 1–2, 3–4, and so on. The next available print’s price updates automatically when you change the number sold. Artist’s proofs remain on enquiry. Blank prices display “Price on enquiry”.</p>
    <div class="toolbar"><label>Collection<select id="price-collection"></select></label><label>Apply to<select id="price-scope"><option value="collection">Entire collection</option><option value="individual">Individual photograph</option></select></label><label id="work-field">Photograph<select id="work"></select></label><label>Format<select id="format"></select></label></div>
    <button type="button" id="edit-collection-details">Edit collection details</button><form id="pricing"><p id="size-summary" class="small"></p><div class="toolbar"><label>Currency<select id="currency"><option>USD</option><option>EUR</option><option>GBP</option><option>CHF</option></select></label><label id="sold-field">Number sold<input id="sold" type="number" min="0" step="1" required /></label></div><p id="collection-price-note" class="small"></p><div id="bands"></div><p id="next-price" class="small"></p><button class="primary">Save prices and availability</button></form>
    <button type="button" id="record-sale" hidden>Record next edition sold</button><p class="small">Record completed sales here, including sales made outside the website. This updates the shared availability record; it does not take payment or reserve a print.</p>
    <p id="missing" class="small" hidden>Set this work’s print dimensions and edition count in the Collection Editor first, then publish the collection. Its formats will appear here after the website rebuilds.</p>
   </section>
   <section id="panel-requests" data-studio-panel="requests" class="panel" hidden><h2>Collector requests</h2><p class="small">Collectors first receive a request acknowledgement. “Approve &amp; email password” sends their separate invitation with a personal password lasting 24 hours from issue. Reissuing invalidates the previous invitation. Revocation also ends existing collector sessions.</p><p class="small"><a href="/editor/collector-email.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Preview collector emails ↗</a></p><button id="refresh">Refresh requests</button><div id="requests"></div></section>
   <section id="panel-mailing" data-studio-panel="mailing" class="panel" hidden><h2>Mailing list</h2><p class="small">Only confirmed subscribers are included in exports. Remove a subscriber when they ask to leave the list. This editor does not send campaigns.</p><button id="export">Export confirmed subscribers</button><div id="subscribers"></div></section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="catalog" set:html={JSON.stringify(catalog).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
 </section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>import '../scripts/editions-editor.js';</script>

<style>
 .studio-actions {display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}
 .studio-actions a {font-size:13px}
 .studio-tabs {display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #b9b5ac;padding-bottom:20px}
 .studio-tabs button[aria-pressed="true"] {background:#24231f;color:#fff}
 #collection-editor-frame {display:block;width:100%;height:850px;border:0;margin-top:20px}
 #edit-collection-details {margin-bottom:20px}
 :global(body.embedded-studio > header), :global(body.embedded-studio > footer), :global(body.embedded-studio .skip-link), :global(body.embedded-studio .studio-tabs), :global(body.embedded-studio .studio-actions a), :global(body.embedded-studio #edit-collection-details) {display:none}
 :global(body.embedded-studio .editions){padding:24px;max-width:none}
</style>
